---- ImageMagick INSTALLATION GUIDE ----

Alright fellas, just a few commands to run : 

-> For Ubuntu / Debian users :
	sudo apt update
	sudo apt upgrade
	sudo apt install imagemagick libmagickwand-dev

-> For Fedora users :
	sudo dnf install ImageMagick ImageMagick-devel

-> For Arch Linux users (take a shower first) : 
	sudo pacman -S imagemagick



Quick verification ! 
run : 
	pkg-config --cflags --libs MagickWand

You should see a few flags like these : 
	-I/usr/include/ImageMagick-7 -lMagickWand-7.Q16HDRI -lMagickCore-7.Q16HDRI



Now let's test it by compiling a C program ! 
Create a test.c file and a test.png file (any image you want)

Now add this code to your test.c file : 

	#include <wand/MagickWand.h>
	#include <stdio.h>

	int main() 
	{
		MagickWandGenesis();
		MagickWand *wand = NewMagickWand();

		if (MagickReadImage(wand, "test.png") == MagickFalse) 
		{
		    printf("Failed to open image\n");
			return 1;
		}

		printf("Image loaded successfully!\n");
		DestroyMagickWand(wand);
		MagickWandTerminus();
		return 0;
	}

Compile it with : 
	gcc test.c -o test $(pkg-config --cflags --libs MagickWand)

And simply run it with : 
	./test

You should get this : "Image loaded successfully!" 
or this "Failed to open image" (If you did not create a test.png file)

Anyways, if there isn't any error message, you should be good to go !

Our gadget is installed ! Thanks Jerry !






