---- TESTING ----

--> preprocess.c : 

Alright let's test preprocess.c ! 
There should be a debugger.c file containing the main() function for this
section of the code.

Make sure you have ImageMagick installed on your device or you won't be able 
to test it. 
Take a look at the installation instructions.

Now, to compile the code, use :
	gcc -g -o debugger debugger.c preprocess.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs MagickWand)

then just run :
	./debugger [TEST FILE]
(there should be a test.png file in the repo).

This is the output you should get for : 

	load_image() : 
		[DEBUG] : Initializing ImageMagick
		[DEBUG] : Called load_image().
		[DEBUG] : load_image() operated succesfully without any error occuring.
		[DEBUG] : Loaded image 735 x 719
		[DEBUG] : Image format: PNG
		[DEBUG] : Success !!
		[DEBUG] : Terminating ImageMagick - Make sure not to call it without re-initializing it !
	

	preprocess_image() :
		[NOT IMPLEMENTED]


